{"skill":{"slug":"2captcha","displayName":"2Captcha"},"version":{"version":"2.0.1","createdAt":1780639726914,"changelog":"- Added a new privacy and authorized use section to documentation, warning users about data sent to 2Captcha.\n- Updated installation instructions to recommend reviewing and cloning the source, rather than using direct install scripts.\n- Clarified supported credential sources for the CLI tool.\n- Removed extraneous documentation file (skill-card.md).","changelogSource":"auto","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"LICENSE","size":1069,"sha256":"aa4bd0c2b9dffc9ec3af63557dfa4b3d2f69c289933a05ca92a3e33cd4ddb3ba","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"README.md","size":5521,"sha256":"53a83e7b2671eb588f9f616fe82075d9d4cedc181319b60807b2bc82d3df3108","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4380,"sha256":"4d0d122339f8b83a8ee3796f4a645a107933c6c61ffa86e60b3d407e97288df5","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"solve-captcha","size":19498,"sha256":"87cb8e28cde060d338134bb1aa12587f8a42390a5708e015e7373bae8f5b4f92","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2150,"sha256":"a8667d6e9419be954e28b859aa17fb29762f2f09886d1403cea2daf538c47f02","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789026716245,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"ce472995f9e77d49be23aabdaccf03e0264ecbd77f8f9baf609af4bc39fdfa05","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/ce472995f9e77d49be23aabdaccf03e0264ecbd77f8f9baf609af4bc39fdfa05","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780642010869},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":62,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":11,"checkedAt":1789026716245},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed 2Captcha command-line helper, with ordinary but important privacy and supply-chain cautions.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Local access is limited to the command arguments, user-specified CAPTCHA image files or URLs, environment variables for terminal behavior, and documented 2Captcha API-key locations.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Installation instructions use mutable sources such as unpinned npx commands and git clone from the default repository branch, so later installs may not match this reviewed artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill clearly discloses that CAPTCHA images, URLs, sitekeys, challenge IDs, task metadata, and the 2Captcha API key are used, and it warns against unapproved sensitive or internal use.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The documented PATH symlink and optional README sudo symlink are visible CLI installation choices, not hidden background persistence; users should avoid privileged or global installs unless needed.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is CAPTCHA solving through 2Captcha, and the bundled Python script implements that directly by submitting user-provided CAPTCHA data and polling for results.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intend to send CAPTCHA content and related page metadata to 2Captcha and its human solvers. Prefer the reviewed bundled script or a pinned commit/release, keep the API key scoped to 2Captcha, avoid sensitive or internal pages unless approved, and skip sudo/global installation unless you specifically need it.","findings":"[PE3] expected: The code reads only the documented 2Captcha API key sources, which is expected for authenticating to the service and is not evidence of broad credential collection.\n[RP1] unexpected: The unpinned installer and clone examples are a real supply-chain caution, but they are installation hygiene issues rather than evidence that the reviewed artifact is malicious.\n[RA2] expected: The reported persistence is a disclosed CLI symlink or API-key config file, not a cron job, service, startup hook, or hidden agent mechanism.\n[PE2] unexpected: The sudo example appears only as an optional README system-wide symlink; it is not required by the skill instructions and should be avoided by most users.\n[LP3] unexpected: The artifact would benefit from a clearer least-privilege/tool-scope section, but its actual data flows and credential locations are disclosed in the skill text and script.\n[T08] unexpected: The static scan's mutable-source concern is supported by the install docs; this warrants user caution but not a Review verdict by itself.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789026716245}}}}}